error: `preed` is not a system function
did you mean `pread`?
error: `declare system function pread` does not match the C function `pread`
`pread` writes into `buf`: declare it `u8[]`, not `readonly u8[]`
C: `ssize_t pread(int fd, void *buf, size_t len, off_t offset)`; Velt: `declare system function pread(fd: i32, buf: u8[], offset: i64): isize;`
`pwrite` only reads `buf`: declare it `readonly u8[]`
`buf` is a buffer: declare it `u8[]`, not `u64` (system functions take no pointers: the array gives the address and the length)
`fd` is a C `int`: declare it `i32`, not `i64`
`close` returns `i32`: declare the result
`path` is a C string: declare it `readonly u8[]` (with one 0 byte, its last), not `string`
`path` is a C string: declare it `readonly u8[]` (with one 0 byte, its last), not `u8[]`
`fsync` takes 1 parameter (fd), not 2
`Bad.nope` is not a field of `struct flock`, which has
`whence` is a C `int`: declare it `i32`, not a function
`length` is a C `off_t`: declare it `i64`, not a floating-point number
`pread` takes 3 parameters (fd, buf, offset), not 5; a part of a buffer is passed as a view: `buf.subarray(start, end)`
`st` is a `struct stat *`: declare it as a `struct` whose fields are fields of `struct stat`, not `Handle`
`declare function fdatasync` is not allowed
`fdatasync` is a system function: `declare system function fdatasync(...)` binds the C library's
a system function is synchronous: `declare system function`, not `async`
